Gizmo the Gnome Warlock cackled as his Succubus, Vixen, lashed a Tiger in Stranglethorn Vale. "More pain, darling!" he shrieked, dodging a swipe. Vixen seduced a nearby Bloodsail Buccaneer, turning him against his crew while Gizmo drained life from the tiger. They were a whirlwind of shadow and charm, clearing quests with terrifying efficiency.

Suddenly, a patrol of elite Gurubashi champions charged. Vixen's soothing kiss failed against their rage; she had no taunt. The elites ignored the dancing demon and focused entirely on the tiny, cloth-clad Gnome. Gizmo's shield shattered instantly. "Wait, I can't hold aggro!" he cried, but it was too late. As darkness closed in, he realized that high damage meant nothing if he died in one hit.

**The Answer:**
Despite the Succubus offering higher damage and utility for solo questing, most Warlocks use Voidwalkers because of **Torment**. In Classic WoW, Warlocks have very low armor and health. Without the Voidwalker's reliable taunt to force enemies to attack the pet instead of the Warlock, the Warlock will die almost instantly when pulling multiple mobs or facing elites. Survival prioritizes threat management over raw DPS. [end of text]


